    "body": "Hi, I guess it's the same problem, so I won't open new issue. I will instead post here.\r\nThe problem is when line_break is disabled.\r\nWhen I press up-arrow to get some command back from the history and then press down-arrow to hide the history, the prompt leaves 3 characters from the command, which looks like an offset issue.\r\nAnd another side-effect is that when the line becomes long enough, it's not wrapped. When you're editing a long line from the history, this makes it impossible to decide where are you editing, because of the offset and the wrap problem.\r\n\r\nHere is a short demo of part of the problem.\r\nhttps://asciinema.org/a/Is72xSFqnYGcVuNvYUQt3xzkx\r\n(EDIT: Unfortunately the video is cropped and the text is not visible on the right. Anyway, I've explained above, so it's not important what I'm typing in the video, it's important to demonstrate the problem)\r\n",
